          "text": "Dear Colleague,\n\n**History of Present Illness:**  \nThe patient has focal epilepsy with onset at age 66. Seizures are focal to bilateral tonic-clonic and currently occur approximately four times per month. The epilepsy has an immune etiology associated with NMDA receptor antibodies and is drug-responsive. MRI demonstrated an incidental lesion.\n\n**Current Medication:**  \n- Carbamazepine, current antiseizure medication\n\n**Seizure Burden:**  \nApproximately four focal to bilateral tonic-clonic seizures per month.\n\n**Assessment:**  \nDrug-responsive focal epilepsy of immune etiology associated with NMDA receptor antibodies, with focal to bilateral tonic-clonic seizures. Incidental lesion noted on MRI.\n\n**Plan:**  \n- Continue carbamazepine.\n- Continue monitoring seizure frequency and clinical response.\n- Follow up in the epilepsy clinic.",
